summary:
- topic: FY2025 Budget Overview
  text: The Superintendent presented the proposed FY2025 budget, which includes a
    5% operating increase and a 3.8% school tax increase, impacting the median homeowner
    by an estimated $123. Key constraints include rising fixed costs and the loss
    of $1.5 million in federal COVID funds that supported 19 positions.
- topic: SPHS Art Teacher Position
  text: 'The administration announced a significant budget adjustment: an SPHS art
    teacher position, previously funded by COVID-era funds, will be moved into the
    local budget. To offset this, a one-year-only teaching position at Dyer School
    will be funded from an elementary school reserve account.'
- topic: Extended Learning Opportunities (ELO)
  text: The Superintendent addressed the ELO coordinator position, which is not in
    the local budget due to an expiring state grant. He assured the Board and community
    that the popular program will continue through a restructured staffing model,
    with more details to be provided before the final budget vote. Board members and
    a parent strongly advocated for the program's continuation.
- topic: Special Education Department
  text: The Director of Special Education presented an overview of the department,
    which serves 649 students. The presentation covered the types of disabilities,
    the range of services provided, the IEP process, and the importance of providing
    services in the least restrictive environment.
- topic: Adult Education Department
  text: The Director of Adult Education highlighted the program's exponential growth,
    making it the third largest in Maine. The program, heavily reliant on grants,
    has expanded its ESOL classes to five levels and is developing digital skills
    and job training programs to meet high community demand.
- topic: Athletics Department
  text: The Athletics Director reviewed the department's 25 high school and 18 middle
    school programs. He highlighted student participation rates (mid-40% at the high
    school), numerous coaching and student awards, and a new partnership with Huddle
    for live-streaming and game analysis.
- topic: Technology Department
  text: The Technology Director detailed plans for FY25, including major infrastructure
    upgrades at the high school (Wi-Fi, switching, cybersecurity), a phased refresh
    of classroom AV technology, and the launch of a new district mobile app to improve
    communication.
- topic: Operations Department
  text: The Director of Operations explained significant budget increases in transportation
    and facilities, attributing them to "right-sizing" previously underfunded lines
    for contract services and utilities. The food service budget is projected to be
    balanced without a fund transfer for the first time in several years.
